cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived correction catalogues, please cite it as below."
title: "SanskritSpellCheck: body-grounded spelling triage for the Cologne Digital Sanskrit Dictionaries"
abstract: >-
  Detectors and a staged triage pipeline for spelling anomalies in digitised Sanskrit
  dictionaries. Headword-level anomaly detection collapses to near-zero precision on
  mature digitised sources; this project confirms candidates against the entry body
  instead, and publishes the resulting do-not-file catalogue that prevents damaging
  bulk corrections across the Cologne corpus.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gasūns
    given-names: Mārcis
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4513-884X"
    email: gasyoun@ya.ru
    affiliation: "Independent scholar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drdhaval2785/SanskritSpellCheck"
# No `license:` key: the project declares no software license (see README "License
# status"), so no SPDX identifier can be stated here truthfully. Adding one would
# invent redistribution terms. This is the same gap as checklist item B2 in
# papers/A44_checklist.md — resolve both together.
keywords:
  - Sanskrit
  - lexicography
  - digital dictionaries
  - spelling error detection
  - grammatical error detection
  - Cologne Digital Sanskrit Dictionaries
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
